\* TIER-2 CERT LEG — baseline safety. EXPECT: clean, and it MUST reach FIXPOINT.
\*
\* Acceptance criterion (PROJECT_STATE §6): this leg is one of the two baselines that
\* must reach a CONCLUSIVE verdict inside the time-box. "Conclusive" for this leg means
\* TLC prints `Model checking completed. No error` — a time-box exit is INCONCLUSIVE and
\* certifies nothing (rule 16).
\*
\* Bounds are IDENTICAL across all six cert legs; the ONLY difference between this file
\* and the four mutation legs is the mutation switch. That is what makes a mutation fire
\* here provably mutation-induced rather than bound-induced (the Mut3Fast/BaselineSafetyFast
\* pairing principle, generalized to the whole cert set).
\*
\* @MAXMSGS@ is substituted by the tlc-cert workflow from the `cert_msgs` dispatch input.
SPECIFICATION Spec

SYMMETRY Sym

CONSTRAINT
CertConstraint

CONSTANTS
Stages = {s1, s2}
MaxEpoch = 1
MaxRId = 1
MaxAttempt = 2
MaxPos = 1
MaxCrashes = 1
MaxMsgs = @MAXMSGS@
EnableUnservable = TRUE
ResetTruncates = TRUE
AttemptFencing = TRUE
AbortGuardEnabled = TRUE

INVARIANTS
Inv
